{
  "id": "genobi-teaser",
  "text": "Make the Genobi teaser: two minutes of the studio in use, cut to the owner's track Trailer-Genobi at its own tempo, at 1920 x 1080, built like the Dimensions mix (a cut written as data that the Director renders). Go through the studio's functions so the viewer sees it work: camera moves onto one readable detail per beat, the pointer and clicks, focus boxes, loaders and generated titles; camera controls at 0:27; the owner's ComfyUI recording with ★ Three.js where the vocal sings it at 0:36; a Paper Shaders beat and the TASTE LAYER credit; the owner's generations on the drops. End on the Genobi end card with the music credit. Nothing is generated, quoted or paid for.",
  "owner": "Koshi",
  "givenOn": "2026-10-30",
  "inputs": {
    "track": "public/media/director-templates/genobi-teaser/teaser-track.mp3",
    "footage": "public/media/director-templates/genobi-teaser/ui-*.mp4 (4K), with the pointer log in docs/genobi-teaser-footage.json; ui-comfy is the owner's own ComfyUI recording and has no log",
    "generations": "the template's media list (shared/templates/genobi-teaser.ts): character, product, audio-visual, dimensions, signal, library-01, library-03, mix-01, mix-02, mix-03",
    "stills": "/media/director-templates/genobi-teaser/still-character.jpg, still-motorbike.jpg and still-bloom.jpg"
  },
  "constraints": [
    "At most 120 s and 128 layers (shots + overlays + the track).",
    "Every cut on the analysed beat grid; shots on whole beats.",
    "On-screen words only from the approved list (docs/genobi-teaser-run/claims.md) unless the owner approves new ones.",
    "Interface shots and words hold at least 1.3 s.",
    "No generation, no quote, no paid call."
  ],
  "storyboard": {
    "why": "The owner's story, segment by segment: what the viewer sees in what order, which actions of each studio recording to show (labels from docs/genobi-teaser-footage.json), where a box or a callout names a detail and which approved words go where. Segment edges are the track's required cuts and the owner's timestamps (camera controls 0:27 = beat 60, Three.js 0:36 = beat 81, out to ComfyUI 0:38 = beat 86). It gives no source times, lengths or overlay numbers for the studio recordings: the run derives those with docs/genobi-teaser-run/decision-table.md. The owner's ComfyUI recording has no capture log, so its source times and moves are the owner's direction, given here.",
